			<div class="content"><blockquote cite="./viewtopic.php?p=1363216&amp;sid=082382ffdbda6450a0ab9ab4a5c7e10a#p1363216"><div><cite><a href="./memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=19438&amp;sid=082382ffdbda6450a0ab9ab4a5c7e10a">andytalaga1</a> wrote: <a href="./viewtopic.php?p=1363216&amp;sid=082382ffdbda6450a0ab9ab4a5c7e10a#p1363216" aria-label="View quoted post" data-post-id="1363216" onclick="if(document.getElementById(hash.substr(1)))href=hash"><i class="icon fa-arrow-circle-up fa-fw" aria-hidden="true"></i></a><span class="responsive-hide">December 13th, 2021, 2:49 pm</span></cite>
Does anyone have the PDFs of the virtual blocks?  These 17 sets are great but it looks like the text and card names were changed somewhat.  For example on GEMP the Galen Starkiller is set 4 (virtual blocks 4 instead of icon 17).  And he references Maris Brood, who in these PDFs that Throdo put up is just called Fallen Jedi. <br>
<br>
Hoping someone can link me or post up the PDFs for Virtual Blocks 1-5 and then Vsets 6.1-9.2 <br>
<br>
Thank you!
</div></blockquote>

You are exactly right.  Previously, the PC hosted the pre-reset blocks on the main page.  Now, they aren't there.  So yes, I will post what I have here.  <em class="text-italics">Please note that I am not sure that these are original releases of these block pdfs.</em>  Some went through changes, and there could have been earlier versions for these.  For example, block 6 had the broken card Rebel Fleet (v).  I originally didn't have the pdf with Rebel Fleet, but after some searching, I found it!  Both versions of block 6 are hosted as attachments below.<br>

